:"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/6408bc19805aa22f940a8198a929d3a6f87f365d","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDY0MDhiYzE5ODA1YWEyMmY5NDBhODE5OGE5MjlkM2E2Zjg3ZjM2NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47","sha":"c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47"}],"sha":"6408bc19805aa22f940a8198a929d3a6f87f365d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/6408bc19805aa22f940a8198a929d3a6f87f365d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:42:31Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:42:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Stop the registration form crashing on the address hierarchy (#468)\n\n* (fix) Pick up the registration address hierarchy crash fix\n\nRegistration white-screens at Matsapha with \"Cannot read properties of\nundefined (reading ''map'')\" whenever the address hierarchy endpoints\nanswer with something other than the array the form expects.\n\nThe addresshierarchy module''s ajax/*.form handlers are legacy Spring\ncontrollers, not REST, and they do not use HTTP status codes to report\nfailure. When the module throws, they answer 200 with the exception\nserialized as JSON - message, localizedMessage, stackTrace, cause - and\nthey can also answer 200 with an empty body. The status is a success, so\nSWR sets no error, and the hooks in address-hierarchy.resource.tsx ran\ndata?.data?.map(...) over undefined or over the exception object.\nAddressComponent then threw during render and took the whole form with\nit.\n\nUpstream #2757 routes all four addresshierarchy hooks through a fetcher\nthat validates the body: a 200 whose body is not the expected array is\nthrown, so SWR reports it through error and AddressComponent renders its\nexisting \"Error occurred fetching ordered fields for address hierarchy\"\nnotification instead of crashing. The derived arrays also fall back to\n[], so a malformed response can no longer throw at a consumer. Where the\nbody is a serialized server exception, the server''s own message is\nsurfaced in the thrown Error - it is the only diagnostic that endpoint\ngives us.\n\n11.1.1-pre.9708 was published on 18 Sep at 21:05 UTC, after #2757 merged\nat 18:42, and is the current next tag. The other six apps move with it\nbecause the monorepo versions its packages together; only the\nregistration app carries a behaviour change we need.\n\nNote this makes the form fail visibly rather than silently - a site whose\naddress hierarchy is broken now shows an error notification in the\naddress section instead of an empty one. The backend bump in the next\ncommit is what stops the endpoint erroring in the first place.\n\n* (fix) Move addresshierarchy to 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT for the ajax endpoint fixes\n\nThe frontend guard in the previous commit stops the registration form\ncrashing, but it turns the crash into an error notification. What makes\nthe endpoint throw in the first place is fixed on the module''s master\nbranch, in three changes that landed after 2.21.0:\n\nADDR-147 (#67) is the one that hits us directly.\ngetChildAddressHierarchyEntries walks the mapped levels assigning one\ntoken per level of the pipe-separated searchString, then returns the\nvalues for the next level down via levels.get(i). Once the caller has\nsupplied a value for every mapped level, i equals levels.size() and that\nlookup throws IndexOutOfBoundsException. The in-loop guard tested\nlevels.size() <= i - 1, one index past the get it was protecting, so it\nnever fired. Since the .form handlers have no exception-to-status\nmapping, the exception reached the browser as 200 with a serialized\nstack trace in the body - exactly the response the frontend was choking\non. It now returns [], as it already did for a level with no children.\nMatsapha configures five levels, so the last one is reached routinely.\n\nADDR-145 (#66) fixes an NPE and, worse, a poisoned cache on a server\nwith no levels configured: getAddressesForLocale published the empty map\ninto fullAddressCache before the loop that threw, so every later search\nfound a map, skipped the build and returned an empty address list as a\nsuccessful response, with nothing that would ever rebuild it.\n\nADDR-144 (#65) fixes an NPE from the unsynchronized resetFullAddressCache\nracing the synchronized cache build, and speeds up large CSV imports -\nour Matsapha and Mosul hierarchies both load this way.\n\nNone of this is released. 2.21.0 is from May 2025 and is still the latest\ntag; the module is not on Maven Central, so mavenrepo.openmrs.org is the\nonly source either way. 2.22.0-SNAPSHOT was last built in May and does\nnot carry these commits - master publishes as 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT, currently\nbuild 13 of 18 Sep. The rest of the diff against 2.21.0 is Spotless\nformatting, license headers and CI migration, so 3.0.0 is a major only by\nbranch convention, not by API break. require_version is 2.7.0 against our\ncore 2.8.9, and resolution is confirmed against the openmrs-repo public\ngroup, which serves snapshots.\n\nThe cost is that the distro is no longer reproducible here: a later\nsnapshot build replaces this one silently. Worth raising a request\nupstream for a 2.22.0 release cutting these three, and pinning that\ninstead.","tree":{"sha":"17b473499111e04ee81c9e82e1f886454d569e8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/17b473499111e04ee81c9e82e1f886454d569e8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47","verification":{"payload":"tree 17b473499111e04ee81c9e82e1f886454d569e8a\nparent 67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1789821751 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789821751 -0700\n\n(fix) Stop the registration form crashing on the address hierarchy (#468)\n\n* (fix) Pick up the registration address hierarchy crash fix\n\nRegistration white-screens at Matsapha with \"Cannot read properties of\nundefined (reading ''map'')\" whenever the address hierarchy endpoints\nanswer with something other than the array the form expects.\n\nThe addresshierarchy module''s ajax/*.form handlers are legacy Spring\ncontrollers, not REST, and they do not use HTTP status codes to report\nfailure. When the module throws, they answer 200 with the exception\nserialized as JSON - message, localizedMessage, stackTrace, cause - and\nthey can also answer 200 with an empty body. The status is a success, so\nSWR sets no error, and the hooks in address-hierarchy.resource.tsx ran\ndata?.data?.map(...) over undefined or over the exception object.\nAddressComponent then threw during render and took the whole form with\nit.\n\nUpstream #2757 routes all four addresshierarchy hooks through a fetcher\nthat validates the body: a 200 whose body is not the expected array is\nthrown, so SWR reports it through error and AddressComponent renders its\nexisting \"Error occurred fetching ordered fields for address hierarchy\"\nnotification instead of crashing. The derived arrays also fall back to\n[], so a malformed response can no longer throw at a consumer. Where the\nbody is a serialized server exception, the server''s own message is\nsurfaced in the thrown Error - it is the only diagnostic that endpoint\ngives us.\n\n11.1.1-pre.9708 was published on 18 Sep at 21:05 UTC, after #2757 merged\nat 18:42, and is the current next tag. The other six apps move with it\nbecause the monorepo versions its packages together; only the\nregistration app carries a behaviour change we need.\n\nNote this makes the form fail visibly rather than silently - a site whose\naddress hierarchy is broken now shows an error notification in the\naddress section instead of an empty one. The backend bump in the next\ncommit is what stops the endpoint erroring in the first place.\n\n* (fix) Move addresshierarchy to 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT for the ajax endpoint fixes\n\nThe frontend guard in the previous commit stops the registration form\ncrashing, but it turns the crash into an error notification. What makes\nthe endpoint throw in the first place is fixed on the module''s master\nbranch, in three changes that landed after 2.21.0:\n\nADDR-147 (#67) is the one that hits us directly.\ngetChildAddressHierarchyEntries walks the mapped levels assigning one\ntoken per level of the pipe-separated searchString, then returns the\nvalues for the next level down via levels.get(i). Once the caller has\nsupplied a value for every mapped level, i equals levels.size() and that\nlookup throws IndexOutOfBoundsException. The in-loop guard tested\nlevels.size() <= i - 1, one index past the get it was protecting, so it\nnever fired. Since the .form handlers have no exception-to-status\nmapping, the exception reached the browser as 200 with a serialized\nstack trace in the body - exactly the response the frontend was choking\non. It now returns [], as it already did for a level with no children.\nMatsapha configures five levels, so the last one is reached routinely.\n\nADDR-145 (#66) fixes an NPE and, worse, a poisoned cache on a server\nwith no levels configured: getAddressesForLocale published the empty map\ninto fullAddressCache before the loop that threw, so every later search\nfound a map, skipped the build and returned an empty address list as a\nsuccessful response, with nothing that would ever rebuild it.\n\nADDR-144 (#65) fixes an NPE from the unsynchronized resetFullAddressCache\nracing the synchronized cache build, and speeds up large CSV imports -\nour Matsapha and Mosul hierarchies both load this way.\n\nNone of this is released. 2.21.0 is from May 2025 and is still the latest\ntag; the module is not on Maven Central, so mavenrepo.openmrs.org is the\nonly source either way. 2.22.0-SNAPSHOT was last built in May and does\nnot carry these commits - master publishes as 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT, currently\nbuild 13 of 18 Sep. The rest of the diff against 2.21.0 is Spotless\nformatting, license headers and CI migration, so 3.0.0 is a major only by\nbranch convention, not by API break. require_version is 2.7.0 against our\ncore 2.8.9, and resolution is confirmed against the openmrs-repo public\ngroup, which serves snapshots.\n\nThe cost is that the distro is no longer reproducible here: a later\nsnapshot build replaces this one silently. Worth raising a request\nupstream for a 2.22.0 release cutting these three, and pinning that\ninstead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqroM3CRC1aQ7uu5