it/67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e","sha":"67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e"}],"sha":"c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/c8fb59cf797dc8bcefee365070322b729b904a47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:36:32Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:36:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Take Active Visits off the Patient Lists page (#465)\n\nactive-visits-widget attaches natively to homepage-widgets-slot only.\npatient-lists-dashboard-slot is rendered by\nopenmrs-esm-patient-list-management-app, so the widget appears on Patient\nLists solely because the distro config adds it there, at every site.\n\nThat add was not deliberate. The block landed in 9af90251 as configure\nonly, against homepage-widgets-slot, gating the widget where it already\nlived:\n\n  \"@openmrs/esm-patient-home-app\": {\n    \"extensionSlots\": {\n      \"homepage-widgets-slot\": {\n        \"configure\": { \"active-visits-widget\": { ... } }\n\n6abb17e7, which migrated to @madiro/esm-home-app, rewrote it: the module\nkey became @openmrs/esm-active-visits-app, the slot became\npatient-lists-dashboard-slot, and add appeared. A placement change buried\nin a dependency-resolution commit.\n\nRestore configure against homepage-widgets-slot and drop the add. This\nalso restores the Configure Visits gate on the home page: Display\nconditions are scoped per slot, so while the block pointed at\npatient-lists-dashboard-slot the home page instance of the widget was\nleft ungated.\n\nFiled under @madiro/esm-home-app, which renders homepage-widgets-slot and\nalready configures homepage-dashboard-slot. The framework flattens\nextensionSlots from every module key and merges by slot name, so the key\ndoes not affect resolution, but keeping it with the rendering app matches\nthe rest of the file. No other config touches homepage-widgets-slot, so\nthere is no merge collision.","tree":{"sha":"bfb79ef7ca38b545202da3afb58844f3723a1a60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/bfb79ef7ca38b545202da3afb58844f3723a1a60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e","verification":{"payload":"tree bfb79ef7ca38b545202da3afb58844f3723a1a60\nparent 1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1789572992 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789572992 -0700\n\n(fix) Take Active Visits off the Patient Lists page (#465)\n\nactive-visits-widget attaches natively to homepage-widgets-slot only.\npatient-lists-dashboard-slot is rendered by\nopenmrs-esm-patient-list-management-app, so the widget appears on Patient\nLists solely because the distro config adds it there, at every site.\n\nThat add was not deliberate. The block landed in 9af90251 as configure\nonly, against homepage-widgets-slot, gating the widget where it already\nlived:\n\n  \"@openmrs/esm-patient-home-app\": {\n    \"extensionSlots\": {\n      \"homepage-widgets-slot\": {\n        \"configure\": { \"active-visits-widget\": { ... } }\n\n6abb17e7, which migrated to @madiro/esm-home-app, rewrote it: the module\nkey became @openmrs/esm-active-visits-app, the slot became\npatient-lists-dashboard-slot, and add appeared. A placement change buried\nin a dependency-resolution commit.\n\nRestore configure against homepage-widgets-slot and drop the add. This\nalso restores the Configure Visits gate on the home page: Display\nconditions are scoped per slot, so while the block pointed at\npatient-lists-dashboard-slot the home page instance of the widget was\nleft ungated.\n\nFiled under @madiro/esm-home-app, which renders homepage-widgets-slot and\nalready configures homepage-dashboard-slot. The framework flattens\nextensionSlots from every module key and merges by slot name, so the key\ndoes not affect resolution, but keeping it with the rendering app matches\nthe rest of the file. No other config touches homepage-widgets-slot, so\nthere is no merge collision.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqreACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcO8QACGesvSKidbgVM5FGPdeEtnz\nlsMkBu4PYq7+3ywMpxf0yWsIL2FKlGFQbA9ZQkTTZ3UI5e4Gr1uGMpkjF7Ri/+NQ\nHcZxEEiEETV8tj5foicAKLyOIvf5b80ViRKyoSXCFuniYd89YXBKIMRONl01xpT3\nOChMsiLIx+F74et23DeKz6mRwOZPMlw/oxH/kg8elmuS59Ugv5iBh0DJA5eSCDiH\nQ8XXyaF8ebVy0iYWWP2div/yf+hYeGAD7ltdZmW0kXS9fyHSkf9luUzsdKDknknN\nsSrKgkiHfd6ByA7CAWhv0cE2tV6WZGY72Yv9ov72sMNY+1W2FvI8oVdXPg7ofcOj\ndiBFBh2PSYdmPZliM2jCUuSmxCuOVDnrNchmzjHPJ8tv1Apk0AkyLipdc/kREk3p\nhc2w8+9GLuNlHQSrgW237TAaha8ts+R9/0UUH7Naq2ycaq8NAsTyejZ7PzMojS54\n0ij/TvEAbW5+GaHxakpWt9TjzrNTPInG7MmvswdYwWpz5ZJwpNUfN2iWulCLpLJO\nPaiYO1NTamuEWQ+y1FRpJ/CWDtEsSKhhdcWnwJOt6TIXUzqyOsdk+/1geNOd3jGo\npYk7qLmbEqhpBX5gMhB+AEIFLEmC3Zg9pBOd5xAvjq/St77MWJB3XQLv7Hy5qNwb\n0p8Zcs9j7l0YIWST2Cgu\n=o02v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T15:36:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDY3YTk1ZjZkMWJmYTI0ZGVhYWE0N2M0ZjM4ZTI4OWNkYjIxOWFiNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef","sha":"1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef"}],"sha":"67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/67a95f6d1bfa24deaaa47c4f38e289cdb219ab4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:31:11Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:31:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Reach the legacy Reporting menu, and give the results viewer full width (#464)\n\n* (fix) Let the data team reach the legacy Reporting menu\n\nThe reporting module''s gutter link is gated on a privilege that nothing\ncreates. GutterListExt.getRequiredPrivilege() returns \"View Reports\", but\nthe module''s config.xml declares only Manage Reports, Manage Report\nDefinitions, Manage Data Set Definitions, Manage Indicator Definitions,\nManage Dimension Definitions, Manage Cohort Definitions, Manage Report\nDesigns, Manage Scheduled Report Tasks and Run Reports. No other module in\nthe distro declares it either, and it is not in core PrivilegeConstants,\nso the link is invisible to everyone except superusers, who bypass\nprivilege checks entirely.\n\nDeclare View Reports in msf_default_privileges.csv. hasPrivilege matches\non name, so defining it makes the module''s check satisfiable.\n\nGrant it to Matsapha: Data Export along with the four reporting\nprivileges the role was missing - Manage Data Set Definitions, Manage\nIndicator Definitions, Manage Dimension Definitions and Manage Scheduled\nReport Tasks. The role now carries all nine privileges the reporting\nmodule declares, so the admin Reporting sections are fully reachable\nrather than partially.\n\nThe admin index sections were already reachable: RunAdminListExt requires\nRun Reports and ManageAdminListExt requires Manage Reports, both of which\nthe role already held. Only the gutter link was blocked.\n\n* (fix) Give the results viewer the full width of the Results tab\n\nSince #456 removed the \"Follow up table demo\" widget from the Results\ntab, the results viewer renders across only half the page.\n\nThe patient chart lays each dashboard slot out as a two-column grid:\n\n  .dashboard            { display: grid;\n                          grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n  .extension:only-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n  .fullWidth            { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n\nand picks the class per extension with\n\n  !!(extension.config?.fullWidth ?? extension.meta?.fullWidth)\n\nso a widget spans both columns only if it declares fullWidth or is the\ngrid''s only child. Of the three extensions in\npatient-chart-test-results-dashboard-slot, obs-table-horizontal-widget and\npatient-flags-list both set meta.fullWidth true; results-viewer declares no\nmeta at all. It has therefore always occupied a single column - the\nfull-width demo table below it filled the page, so the gap was not\nvisible. Removing the table left the viewer beside empty space.\n\nSet fullWidth through the slot''s configure block, which the component\nreads ahead of meta. Applied to the same three sites as #456.\n\nNote for testers: the framework logs \"Unknown config key ... Ignoring.\"\nfor this key because it is not in a declared config schema. The value is\nstill applied - setDefaults clones the provided config before layering\nschema defaults, so unknown keys survive into extension.config.","tree":{"sha":"f0deb4775e830919a101c456ac0b15b57c552554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/f0deb4775e830919a101c456ac0b15b57c552554"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef","verification":{"payload":"tree f0deb4775e830919a101c456ac0b15b57c552554\nparent d3b3ce2beda62c5e700993cef043ebba515b7a98\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1789565471 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789565471 -0700\n\n(fix) Reach the legacy Reporting menu, and give the results viewer full width (#464)\n\n* (fix) Let the data team reach the legacy Reporting menu\n\nThe reporting module''s gutter link is gated on a privilege that nothing\ncreates. GutterListExt.getRequiredPrivilege() returns \"View Reports\", but\nthe module''s config.xml declares only Manage Reports, Manage Report\nDefinitions, Manage Data Set Definitions, Manage Indicator Definitions,\nManage Dimension Definitions, Manage Cohort Definitions, Manage Report\nDesigns, Manage Scheduled Report Tasks and Run Reports. No other module in\nthe distro declares it either, and it is not in core PrivilegeConstants,\nso the link is invisible to everyone except superusers, who bypass\nprivilege checks entirely.\n\nDeclare View Reports in msf_default_privileges.csv. hasPrivilege matches\non name, so defining it makes the module''s check satisfiable.\n\nGrant it to Matsapha: Data Export along with the four reporting\nprivileges the role was missing - Manage Data Set Definitions, Manage\nIndicator Definitions, Manage Dimension Definitions and Manage Scheduled\nReport Tasks. The role now carries all nine privileges the reporting\nmodule declares, so the admin Reporting sections are fully reachable\nrather than partially.\n\nThe admin index sections were already reachable: RunAdminListExt requires\nRun Reports and ManageAdminListExt requires Manage Reports, both of which\nthe role already held. Only the gutter link was blocked.\n\n* (fix) Give the results viewer the full width of the Results tab\n\nSince #456 removed the \"Follow up table demo\" widget from the Results\ntab, the results viewer renders across only half the page.\n\nThe patient chart lays each dashboard slot out as a two-column grid:\n\n  .dashboard            { display: grid;\n                          grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n  .extension:only-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n  .fullWidth            { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n\nand picks the class per extension with\n\n  !!(extension.config?.fullWidth ?? extension.meta?.fullWidth)\n\nso a widget spans both columns only if it declares fullWidth or is the\ngrid''s only child. Of the three extensions in\npatient-chart-test-results-dashboard-slot, obs-table-horizontal-widget and\npatient-flags-list both set meta.fullWidth true; results-viewer declares no\nmeta at all. It has therefore always occupied a single column - the\nfull-width demo table below it filled the page, so the gap was not\nvisible. Removing the table left the viewer beside empty space.\n\nSet fullWidth through the slot''s configure block, which the component\nreads ahead of meta. Applied to the same three sites as #456.\n\nNote for testers: the framework logs \"Unknown config key ... Ignoring.\"\nfor this key because it is not in a declared config schema. The value is\nstill applied - setDefaults clones the provided config before layering\nschema defaults, so unknown keys survive into extension.config.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqpofCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdU4QAE9wlIPtLwVTdS5T1tdvhcxG\nrxxuyer5JOu0T+Dhr73rFpZH40/GpZF/DnB8N2ihAcGkEpA8NuYpsk7983zSf1Tr\npq96fEL7beqqC0X5fVyHIfo+ZMy+O+z+ogBWqIYZr83AAgpE364n/Noxyt7E7zRl\nMhRooiQnyeVyqK6fENTytefk9qDbmObQkWY3C2UlkLOtbry4J8S276zlHAIn31Q2\nxtqqctvu2VC6rZrP5N2SjGsSoXskcE/XH8pRDKTuanRddYJtqMEuEhD7K+NJ6sJC\nZtIU5PVxZ2dNnN9uJ1sgrmZU1fc/YcGronM7ow+RgyJ4nK49SCbL8f6E12lTVeL+\nVdzwvVskzOAPGmeMFeXq5YwUOoTwoey/GSsYd46azmRcAY0VbdbAazr2qeQlrKrp\nqtxdcMG0cj5t9Yjm566BlNSdlRMeW00dVpil3rIYOrX297700m/CryTfL8tTJEGv\nHGkkmnnCKMHfpsiKyUZkxSYE1bQGbdgXKvJMxndoJRyCvyiAw82LuWzQEZccudPy\nA4zI7t1EQJdaX/bpJhadX4LhWFq9bBajAy6SB3sONCzr8BqPwnfueGIuiI3dOFAR\nmMxQcysp8YOYmktJirwa0TOZmDhaAZyPi1OvozmOyIU0j1q8Bz5m/Gx2RGW9SH0l\n8FgT6CyfFhwFmW0DxS15\n=sS2P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T13:31:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDFjMDA5MTE5MTc2NDRjODRlZGIzZWNhZWRjYjY1NDA3ZTJmNjNiZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/d3b3ce2beda62c5e700993cef043ebba515b7a98","sha":"d3b3ce2beda62c5e700993cef043ebba515b7a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/d3b3ce2beda62c5e700993cef043ebba515b7a98"}],"sha":"1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/1c00911917644c84edb3ecaedcb65407e2f63bef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/d3b3ce2beda62c5e700993cef043ebba515b7a98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T01:25:40Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T01:25:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Restore registration and legacy admin access for non-admin users (#463)\n\nRegistration fails with \"cannot read properties of undefined\" for any\nuser who does not inherit General Doctor - at Matsapha that is the three\nreception accounts, whose whole job is registration.\n\nThe form fetches /addresstemplate, /location, /relationshiptype and\n/metadatamapping/termmapping before it renders, and reads the responses\nunguarded. The primary identifier type lookup does\n\n  t?.data?.results[0]?.metadataUuid\n\nwhere results is optional-chained but [0] is not, so a 403 throws rather\nthan surfacing a permission error. General role carries none of the four\nprivileges those calls need. Patient registration now does, along with\nEdit Relationships and Delete Relationships for the POST and DELETE the\nform makes on /relationship/{uuid} - it previously granted Add\nRelationships without even Get Relationship Types.\n\nThe reads sit on Patient registration rather than General role so that\nGet Global Properties, which exposes every global property over REST, is\nlimited to accounts that register patients. Clinical staff already hold\nall four through General Doctor.\n\nSeparately, nobody but the superuser can open the legacy admin site.\nlegacyui''s admin/index.jsp requires View Administration Functions and\nredirects to /login.htm when it is missing, so an unprivileged user is\nshown the login form again and a missing privilege looks exactly like a\nrejected password - no password reset can clear it. No role in the distro\nheld it, not even Supervisor, which carries Manage Modules, Manage Global\nProperties, Manage Roles and 80+ other legacy admin privileges it could\nnever reach. Grant it to Supervisor and to Matsapha: Data Export.\n\nMatsapha: Registration Supervisor inherits Patient registration. It\ngranted six delete privileges with no ability to register, or even read a\nrelationship type, so it was incoherent on its own. All five holders are\nalready assigned Patient registration directly in provisioning, so no\nuser gains access.","tree":{"sha":"f25a96626ba182aea76eb6fab200f55c4350a55c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/f25a96626ba182aea76eb6fab200f55c4350a55c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/d3b3ce2beda62c5e700993cef043ebba515b7a98","verification":{"payload":"tree f25a96626ba182aea76eb6fab200f55c4350a55c\nparent a21b04515ed955988bf2fb8875339c3cfccfa932\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1789521940 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789521940 -0700\n\n(fix) Restore registration and legacy admin access for non-admin users (#463)\n\nRegistration fails with \"cannot read properties of undefined\" for any\nuser who does not inherit General Doctor - at Matsapha that is the three\nreception accounts, whose whole job is registration.\n\nThe form fetches /addresstemplate, /location, /relationshiptype and\n/metadatamapping/termmapping before it renders, and reads the responses\nunguarded. The primary identifier type lookup does\n\n  t?.data?.results[0]?.metadataUuid\n\nwhere results is optional-chained but [0] is not, so a 403 throws rather\nthan surfacing a permission error. General role carries none of the four\nprivileges those calls need. Patient registration now does, along with\nEdit Relationships and Delete Relationships for the POST and DELETE the\nform makes on /relationship/{uuid} - it previously granted Add\nRelationships without even Get Relationship Types.\n\nThe reads sit on Patient registration rather than General role so that\nGet Global Properties, which exposes every global property over REST, is\nlimited to accounts that register patients. Clinical staff already hold\nall four through General Doctor.\n\nSeparately, nobody but the superuser can open the legacy admin site.\nlegacyui''s admin/index.jsp requires View Administration Functions and\nredirects to /login.htm when it is missing, so an unprivileged user is\nshown the login form again and a missing privilege looks exactly like a\nrejected password - no password reset can clear it. No role in the distro\nheld it, not even Supervisor, which carries Manage Modules, Manage Global\nProperties, Manage Roles and 80+ other legacy admin privileges it could\nnever reach. Grant it to Supervisor and to Matsapha: Data Export.\n\nMatsapha: Registration Supervisor inherits Patient registration. It\ngranted six delete privileges with no ability to register, or even read a\nrelationship type, so it was incoherent on its own. All five holders are\nalready assigned Patient registration directly in provisioning, so no\nuser gains access.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SI