l":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c","sha":"85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c"}],"sha":"f71c4f58d08f88ad5aeb921ce059d32a0e146b17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/f71c4f58d08f88ad5aeb921ce059d32a0e146b17"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T11:52:47Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T11:52:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"LIME2-1285 Autoclose all Matsapha visit types (#455)\n\nPR #447 (e940c29) intended to extend auto-close to every Matsapha visit\ntype, but pasted the Matsapha list into Mosul''s scheduler config instead.\nMatsapha''s own property was never updated, so it kept the value from\n09c2ca0: OPD Visit, Facility Visit, Home Visit, Offline Visit, Group\nSession. Those names come verbatim from the RefApp demo package\n(01_referenceapplication-demo/visittypes-core_data.csv) and no visit type\nby those names exists at Matsapha, so auto-close silently did nothing.\n\nmatsapha: list the 14 visit types the site actually defines. Verified\nagainst the running instance - visit_type holds exactly these rows, none\nretired, and the deployed configuration mounts only the site''s own\nvisittypes directory (no distro or RefApp types are loaded).\n\nmosul: revert to the pre-e940c29 value, OPD Visit, Home Visit, Telehealth.\nHome Visit is not in mosul_visittypes.csv but does exist in production, so\nit stays. ER Visit and IPD Visit are left out, as before.","tree":{"sha":"2ac4544a17063d489186d5dd0635dcb7c88bb910","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/2ac4544a17063d489186d5dd0635dcb7c88bb910"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ac4544a17063d489186d5dd0635dcb7c88bb910\nparent 176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788954767 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788954767 -0700\n\nLIME2-1285 Autoclose all Matsapha visit types (#455)\n\nPR #447 (e940c29) intended to extend auto-close to every Matsapha visit\ntype, but pasted the Matsapha list into Mosul''s scheduler config instead.\nMatsapha''s own property was never updated, so it kept the value from\n09c2ca0: OPD Visit, Facility Visit, Home Visit, Offline Visit, Group\nSession. Those names come verbatim from the RefApp demo package\n(01_referenceapplication-demo/visittypes-core_data.csv) and no visit type\nby those names exists at Matsapha, so auto-close silently did nothing.\n\nmatsapha: list the 14 visit types the site actually defines. Verified\nagainst the running instance - visit_type holds exactly these rows, none\nretired, and the deployed configuration mounts only the site''s own\nvisittypes directory (no distro or RefApp types are loaded).\n\nmosul: revert to the pre-e940c29 value, OPD Visit, Home Visit, Telehealth.\nHome Visit is not in mosul_visittypes.csv but does exist in production, so\nit stays. ER Visit and IPD Visit are left out, as before.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoUiPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8l4QACJJ3Tt+BZXChdGeI+9RVEjt\nTV4zy2qRlmhOmNFY4tUMOxvnJM55MDJz8mfOT4oriHR0IzR9XZZ4wGX+b6V/MeXD\nZE66CUnIjTXdnpStojAV5E6Bh0+wtljiVcEdoWPWGS5VbAgLOYqFdQHasHiILGOf\nDfgp6h67YgQwyv4OoRAXzvRAvMkmQttPXqQrUBZLxtKahfK4rQeruViHQa/WzW6u\ncMdbt1yPalZFY2NmmZ4O1IyTV+pfmTpx/ogUtvHR4gQq/+o/ctbOdEa32FgW8n2Y\n5WLlV/qqNfPaWE5lXf63b56BUJ4YZ7r1W7ybX25uclStYVgKKWzMw3huGYTG49pV\nXCY7+BGu8sdMD5vanRT/BYQyc0x+f9E6Bbd38P+n/DfTGVkD33H/fHZMnU2B0At0\nz5aNuiuGDqpKEGf6BfyvINVXno/J+w9yAu6iRNdUK49gIeFWn+JpWTQfDUGodDbs\nBvidr1j9nL0JB2dEVfMZvkkhCfnP38F/41hQthIbEaiobTOnqU8qnHsSJSa70aKj\nauBgbGP6s/faj5Uef7K/p5UCbKNdSLolLjN6AmLawTnNXeD1t5sIfaPS8/wp0iZ5\n6N8/htSbHGGw3vrgYNe6jt3supv5XbDPke12CQjKkICJC48vW53xV8bK9mM1dQ9F\n75MHTYzw7Z8uu2LKqmU9\n=rLyX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T11:52:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDg1ZGU0YWY3NjJiMDhhNWRiNWY4MGY4MWU2ZTZkMzhlZDAyMzViMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2","sha":"176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2"}],"sha":"85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/85de4af762b08a5db5f80f81e6e6d38ed0235b0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T11:17:37Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T11:17:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"LIME2-1290 Restore commonreports module so default reports are installed (#454)\n\nThe default reports (Patients, Visits, Encounters, Observations,\nOrders, Conditions, Concepts, Programs, Appointments, Audit, Diagnoses,\nPatient History) were absent from every site. Only two report\ndefinitions existed, both from our own patientdocuments module.\n\nThe \"Add MSF addons to ozone\" antrun step deletes every Ozone-supplied\nomod except serialization*, and each module is then re-added by explicit\ndependency here. commonreports, which provides the default report\ndefinitions, was never re-declared, so it was deleted and never came\nback.\n\nBoth the delete step and the patientsummary dependency were introduced\ntogether in 8cbada8 (Upgrade OpenMRS to RefApp 3.4.0). patientsummary\nexists in the distro solely as a commonreports dependency - no other\ninstalled module requires it - so commonreports itself was simply\noverlooked when that module list was rebuilt.\n\nTwo other pieces of config already assume the module is present:\nreporting.serializer.whitelist.types whitelists\norg.openmrs.module.commonreports.**, and Mosul''s liquibase.xml\nreferences a commonreports renderer class.\n\nVersion requirements are satisfied by the current stack: commonreports\n1.5.0 needs reporting >= 1.21.0 (we ship 2.1.0), initializer >= 2.1.0\n(2.12.0) and patientsummary >= 2.2.0 (2.2.0). No activation config is\nneeded - each report is gated on report.<name>.active, which defaults\nto true.\n\nVerified end to end: built the distro and the Matsapha site, wiped\nserialized_object and the reporting.reportManager.* properties, and\nrestarted. All 14 report definitions installed with no errors, and\nreportingrest serves them.","tree":{"sha":"c176b5b6f0788c46c8ae4f6adf7b794b003ebe4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/c176b5b6f0788c46c8ae4f6adf7b794b003ebe4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2","verification":{"payload":"tree c176b5b6f0788c46c8ae4f6adf7b794b003ebe4f\nparent 17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788952657 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788952657 -0700\n\nLIME2-1290 Restore commonreports module so default reports are installed (#454)\n\nThe default reports (Patients, Visits, Encounters, Observations,\nOrders, Conditions, Concepts, Programs, Appointments, Audit, Diagnoses,\nPatient History) were absent from every site. Only two report\ndefinitions existed, both from our own patientdocuments module.\n\nThe \"Add MSF addons to ozone\" antrun step deletes every Ozone-supplied\nomod except serialization*, and each module is then re-added by explicit\ndependency here. commonreports, which provides the default report\ndefinitions, was never re-declared, so it was deleted and never came\nback.\n\nBoth the delete step and the patientsummary dependency were introduced\ntogether in 8cbada8 (Upgrade OpenMRS to RefApp 3.4.0). patientsummary\nexists in the distro solely as a commonreports dependency - no other\ninstalled module requires it - so commonreports itself was simply\noverlooked when that module list was rebuilt.\n\nTwo other pieces of config already assume the module is present:\nreporting.serializer.whitelist.types whitelists\norg.openmrs.module.commonreports.**, and Mosul''s liquibase.xml\nreferences a commonreports renderer class.\n\nVersion requirements are satisfied by the current stack: commonreports\n1.5.0 needs reporting >= 1.21.0 (we ship 2.1.0), initializer >= 2.1.0\n(2.12.0) and patientsummary >= 2.2.0 (2.2.0). No activation config is\nneeded - each report is gated on report.<name>.active, which defaults\nto true.\n\nVerified end to end: built the distro and the Matsapha site, wiped\nserialized_object and the reporting.reportManager.* properties, and\nrestarted. All 14 report definitions installed with no errors, and\nreportingrest serves them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoUBRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK8MQACV21HzE2LawDgj6oQ007OKm\nlSM6MvCYbyccY7aXnrKiMzN0DCBZK2oKYAr/yD5vWhK3LERW2vm5QtPNNtQ30cK1\nkrkoAmRxvgnCkMCp+rT239s3EudbZyJlNwH/IztqLNiQUsUEShuDMwsNNL5jTxZN\nscx7TCdKH05WGY4LyEAAvBR1WGxOmuxNPMdlyHb1kkmkOa4eD75PvASnC10DJ86q\nc/67BERIXkrIYwGIlKwF/3AOZR8uOSN2g4Id07IuPEGyN/czwgcvQnNQbFnU5EZb\ncWXUcEy5y+7/UlPosYXp39HfaaQYqZI53a2Mppf72kr7/zD9haogYzjnGqlbn6vI\niVz2QouadAPAk2mYZVfXHjy13aBCH+y1Qc5/D0S1Mru5ac87mhvPb0tUh7VPb0vV\n1KSd6XnosKtsTd00oLayJ7st7RHij71Hx05SaGJGOsMkyVCoPtiMoMubsxuU/s+g\nl3r63mipz5IVXCzCWqi7ub5xJA438VRsig+uDyTXhlIVHPVKMrYP02gjNfdF7v1Z\n+4VCBXDxCaklnAt3j0JDTBWv/6PiQz/KJM+BkSozPSoX31RrTJBmDIA3OIdiV2NS\n41oXcPWiUr1KXj53BxJdCcxYSgDsBvzbwXD8bOohsjrtdsFNwYz+6oJQ48Nk5B3A\nsyQgdkbBx2w5zRdgy5ZW\n=Nr1g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T11:17:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDE3NmIzNzhmZDk0ZDVjZjgxYmU4NGMxOTljNjIzNjBiYjY4ODE0ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b","sha":"17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b"}],"sha":"176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/176b378fd94d5cf81be84c199c62360bb68814d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:18:54Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:18:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"LIME2-1291 Fix address hierarchy never loading at Matsapha (#453)\n\n* LIME2-1294 Rollback appointments package to release version\n\n* LIME2-1291 Fix address hierarchy never loading at Matsapha\n\nThe address dropdowns at Matsapha were empty because the address\nhierarchy was never imported: both address_hierarchy_level and\naddress_hierarchy_entry were empty, and the backend logged\n\n  AddressConfigurationLoader - Address hierarchy configuration file\n  appears invalid, skipping the loading process:\n  /openmrs/data/configuration/addresshierarchy/addressConfiguration.xml\n\nThe \"Copy local initializer_config with content-package structure\"\nbuild step rewrites every domain as <domain>/<file> ->\n<domain>/<artifactId>/<file>. That is correct for Initializer domains,\nwhich scan sub-directories as content packages, but addresshierarchy is\nnot an Initializer domain. It is loaded by the Address Hierarchy\nmodule''s own AddressConfigurationLoader, which resolves\naddressConfiguration.xml against the domain directory root only and\nnever recurses. The config was therefore invisible and silently skipped.\n\nExclude addresshierarchy from the content-package mapper and copy it\nflat instead. The nesting arrived in 903783b (ozone alpha.15) and\napplies to all three sites, so all three are fixed. Mosul and Bunia show\nno symptom today only because their entries were imported before that\nchange and persist in their databases; their address config is equally\ndead for any future edit.\n\nAlso drop the header row from addresshierarchy_matsapha.csv. The\nimporter treats it as data, so it created one bogus entry at every\nlevel - \"country\" showed up as a selectable country alongside\n\"Eswatini\". Mosul and Bunia have no such header.\n\nVerified by rebuilding from source, wiping the hierarchy tables and the\nloader checksums, and restarting against the build artifact: 5 levels\nload with no loader error, and the endpoints the registration form\ncalls cascade correctly (Eswatini -> 4 regions -> 23 inkhundla under\nManzini), with no bogus entries.\n\nNote for deployment: addressConfiguration.xml sets <wipe>true</wipe>, so\nthe first boot after this lands will delete and re-import the address\nhierarchy on already-provisioned sites.","tree":{"sha":"c3050e79a4e0b627ceaa44427864ed2ba9ab9c4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/c3050e79a4e0b627ceaa44427864ed2ba9ab9c4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b","verification":{"payload":"tree c3050e79a4e0b627ceaa44427864ed2ba9ab9c4e\nparent 2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788945534 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788945534 -0700\n\nLIME2-1291 Fix address hierarchy never loading at Matsapha (#453)\n\n* LIME2-1294 Rollback appointments package to release version\n\n* LIME2-1291 Fix address hierarchy never loading at Matsapha\n\nThe address dropdowns at Matsapha were empty because the address\nhierarchy was never imported: both address_hierarchy_level and\naddress_hierarchy_entry were empty, and the backend logged\n\n  AddressConfigurationLoader - Address hierarchy configuration file\n  appears invalid, skipping the loading process:\n  /openmrs/data/configuration/addresshierarchy/addressConfiguration.xml\n\nThe \"Copy local initializer_config with content-package structure\"\nbuild step rewrites every domain as <domain>/<file> ->\n<domain>/<artifactId>/<file>. That is correct for Initializer domains,\nwhich scan sub-directories as content packages, but addresshierarchy is\nnot an Initializer domain. It is loaded by the Address Hierarchy\nmodule''s own AddressConfigurationLoader, which resolves\naddressConfiguration.xml against the domain directory root only and\nnever recurses. The config was therefore invisible and silently skipped.\n\nExclude addresshierarchy from the content-package mapper and copy it\nflat instead. The nesting arrived in 903783b (ozone alpha.15) and\napplies to all three sites, so all three are fixed. Mosul and Bunia show\nno symptom today only because their entries were imported before that\nchange and persist in their databases; their address config is equally\ndead for any future edit.\n\nAlso drop the header row from addresshierarchy_matsapha.csv. The\nimporter treats it as data, so it created one bogus entry at every\nlevel - \"country\" showed up as a selectable country alongside\n\"Eswatini\". Mosul and Bunia have no such header.\n\nVerified by rebuilding from source, wiping the hierarchy tables and the\nloader checksums, and restarting against the build artifact: 5 levels\nload with no loader error, and the endpoints the registration form\ncalls cascade correctly (Eswatini -> 4 regions -> 23 inkhundla under\nManzini), with no bogus entries.\n\nNote for deployment: addressConfiguration.xml sets <wipe>true</wipe>, so\nthe first boot after this lands will delete and re-import the address\nhierarchy on already-provisioned sites.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoSR+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm3sQAF3CmCYV3/OI0fhwkhecT5+2\nIoTEWJGeRT7IJs5r41ZcIvYHsXihqY8I/Eb5jvhMUvS8Csml92vaB6Ep5ynw+9Sl\n/Sl/4AvlOXTmI6oHdnFKpev4k4ds/wBVKBRd6nUDMKY1O9sqSL/trgV6mj4RKAd6\nfit+r3zF0ir+p9Fl28FUpOOMzGlCTim52FSgZHmA7kdfJthDiloNdI5QnLrhu+mb\nnrbm7IYBHo/b14G9GWQgC9IGYsf2LJu+Q8edN7nq7e5f77xG17Xn3ZZiFEy4lJ+O\nMqggGnJ4+40TNCE5phE10RUZb6Vrv1VscRO2O+pCZAHSuF5NKkJ4Xha5B5c3+loP\nR1vzg2Hc8QX2Z5HKrFxn7xbCK74sEFzHHwEMjss7jh6khzRKAwVXRjtsj7+QdxOI\nr0k427cQNgvK5Z1q3e/Do+9jG9FHV0w0XJ5s8DqDoK+v5MzjUQzhQ8zsIUy9+Kd1\nsNAwaQwVxCKO1CEzOiiJ2wfKZRu61hR3LA/6ib+1PMOwyH2z4GkdrNrNhMWxUI/f\nfvK3ZY3WJvlOzHcVLqH5q2xId4F55YJl9YMoexUe1YA5tjJiF4Z10Zx5Y2bbCihr\nPzRcvIjP1XiSfWTutUEWajNtlxvI5SbUrz/r9tZEeygOcwyNd2XLKg6i2r0J+8/o\nqqrhMlS5e4e6jfiSCK16\n=8mFG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T09:18:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDE3ZDFiMWZjNTVkMTM3MWVkZDcxZWM4OTBlNDhmNDczYzI0OGM1MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b","sha":"2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b"}],"sha":"17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/17d1b1fc55d1371edd71ec890e48f473c248c51b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:10:56Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:10:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(feat) Define the Matsapha site roles in Initializer (#452)\n\nThe three \"Matsapha: ...\" site roles exist only because\nLIME-EMR-Tooling/Users/matsapha/Matsapha_Users_202609011600.sql creates them.\nThat makes a role definition depend on somebody remembering to run a script by\nhand against each database, and it means the privileges a clinician holds are\nnot reproducible from this repository.\n\nMove them into Initializer as a site-scoped roles CSV. The privileges are\ncarried over unchanged - 6 for Registration Supervisor, 8 for Data Export, 35\nfor Clinical - and each role keeps an empty Inherited roles column, matching the\nflat model the SQL deliberately used: the distro domain roles all inherit\nGeneral Doctor, which carries Manage Roles, Manage Modules, Manage Global\nProperties, Delete Users and Edit User Passwords, and a clinician filling in a\nfamily planning form should not also be able to edit roles.\n\nThe original UUIDs are reused, so on sites already provisioned by the SQL script\nInitializer updates the existing rows rather than creating a second copy.\n\nSite-scoped rather than appended to distro_roles.csv: these roles are specific to\nMatsapha and every site loads the distro file.\n\nThe matching change in LIME-EMR-Tooling reduces the SQL script to creating\naccounts and assigning roles. Deploy this first - the roles must exist before\nthat script can assign them.","tree":{"sha":"e6b696dc7940be8098be35ca37cc0bf2e6a1aca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/e6b696dc7940be8098be35ca37cc0bf2e6a1aca2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b","verification":{"payload":"tree e6b696dc7940be8098be35ca37cc0bf2e6a1aca2\nparent 16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788811856 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788811856 -0700\n\n(feat) Define the Matsapha site roles in Initializer (#452)\n\nThe three \"Matsapha: ...\" site roles exist only because\nLIME-EMR-Tooling/Users/matsapha/Matsapha_Users_202609011600.sql creates them.\nThat makes a role definition depend on somebody remembering to run a script by\nhand against each database, and it means the privileges a clinician holds are\nnot reproducible from this repository.\n\nMove them into Initializer as a site-scoped roles CSV. The privileges are\ncarried over unchanged - 6 for Registration Supervisor, 8 for Data Export, 35\nfor Clinical - and each role keeps an empty Inherited roles column, matching the\nflat model the SQL deliberately used: the distro domain roles all inherit\nGeneral Doctor, which carries Manage Roles, Manage Modules, Manage Global\nProperties, Delete Users and Edit User Passwords, and a clinician filling in a\nfamily planning form should not also be able to edit roles.\n\nThe original UUIDs are reused, so on sites already provisioned by the SQL script\nInitializer updates the existing rows rather than creating a second copy.\n\nSite-scoped rather than appended to distro_roles.csv: these roles are specific to\nMatsapha and every site loads the distro file.\n\nThe matching change in LIME-EMR-Tooling reduces the SQL script to creating\naccounts and assigning roles. Deploy this first - the roles must exist before\nthat script can assign them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnxpQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/xEQAE6q5k7kMjx0QovZHDDkhU35\nTeoWoIJz6ZdhQ+ynfD+H74H2ffuL6mXwbSEFXqBFovlc+rQ0N+WlFAiIx4jhVkqG\nt8+wK6n8XFsljEl8c07roe4E3aTbyTod+yZ/r5ftOBNwAMI3D5yjCGVDVoHP3HyD\nqIEWA2miNcwhh5HkLtz3TlNyZABkCWI36heZX21m1naLLTEv7v8v9jL0Z7jkwRxv\nprUvhiXrvijeh0+uUve8rZ7PZQ91mZDcxeKK26uoDB0xKIrdNcyh35z9b03LqIvl\ni0m6ZYxtlCBnmE7Jv+CS+OJRJ3nrcIZyTAtRxmszzqE3w5RezeQFeDDpNiI/3ydS\nKx1vx0/11jmGg6oLE8stXDxc+F6pFeAEBtapdEPfMy2fXonsVSFZpL+QvCLL/vxm\n8mrbILyBaGE4IrYeOqZgc3bz54lZo8OGpTuHPTrWcrR/RktKss3TvC9QS4T+Mo1s\ngMtd6rQAQcY9lDAd13UT0EWmwMcMwwj15540lt6Q32ZkBmgVwBnXv4XB9Vi/e+wC\niUmLMXAKKuL8XPn89o4WBEZl1QWrG0ftr5yLwzvsG1FtCRrgD++GeO//PiberLCU\nK62JgKtv0TmOrDmuayNMAybmi+BEMQFXeAbcOEa1HtzL2xLXCJRq0KiwQqBGWdaZ\nXJkf2fghVpOShFfQOw17\n=xuKB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T20:10:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDJlNjg4ZjE2N2VlNGZlYTUxZWYyZDcyNTA4YTBmZTI3OWM1NjAzMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c","sha":"16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c"}],"sha":"2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/2e688f167ee4fea51ef2d72508a0fe279c56030b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T21:49:12Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T21:49:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Stop the patient chart crashing and restore clinical privileges (#451)\n\n* (fix) Strip disabled frontend modules from the routes registry too\n\nOpening a patient chart crashed the browser tab for non-admin users at\nMatsapha. The renderer died after logging\n\n  Could not find the package @madiro/esm-nutrition-app defined in the\n  current importmap\n\n457,406 times in a single page load.\n\nremove-importmap-entries.groovy deleted the modules named by the\n`modulesToRemove` property from importmap.json but left them declared in\nroutes.registry.json. The deployed build therefore advertised 42 apps\nwhile the importmap could resolve only 39. Matsapha disables three\n(@madiro/esm-mental-health-app, @madiro/esm-nutrition-app and\n@openmrs/esm-ward-app), and the nutrition app registers an extension into\npatient-chart-dashboard-slot - a slot that renders only on the chart,\nwhich is why home and patient search were unaffected and only clicking\nthrough to a patient broke.\n\nThe app-shell retried resolving those packages without bound until the\ntab ran out of memory. Bunia and Mosul use the same script and had the\nsame latent inconsistency.\n\nThe script now strips both files, discards the stale .br/.gz copies\nwritten before the edit (they still held the pre-removal content, so\nnginx could serve an importmap that disagreed with the plain file), and\nfails the build if any app is left declared in routes.registry.json\nwithout an importmap entry.\n\n* (fix) Restore the chart read privileges clinical users need\n\nEvery Matsapha user hit 403s across the patient chart. Fourteen\nprivileges were missing from `General role`:\n\n  Edit Users              recently-viewed patients (regression from #449)\n  Get Allergies           allergies tab\n  Get Conditions          conditions tab\n  Get Diagnoses           visit note diagnoses\n  Get Programs            programs tab\n  Get Patient Programs    programs tab\n  Get Forms               clinical forms list\n  Get Care Settings       orders tab and lab worklists\n  Get Orders              orders tab\n  Get Order Types         ordering\n  Get Order Frequencies   drug ordering\n  Get Encounter Roles     saving a form\n  Get Medication Dispense dispensing\n  Get Notes               visit notes\n\nOnly `Edit Users` was a regression from #449, which moved it to\n`Supervisor`. The other thirteen were never on `General role` - they live\non `General Doctor`, which no Matsapha user holds, because the site''s\nprovisioning script builds flat `Matsapha:` roles instead of using the\ndistro domain roles.\n\n`Patient registration` gains `Add Relationships` so registration clerks\ncan record relationships; the role previously carried no privileges of\nits own.\n\nNote that granting `Edit Users` lets any holder edit any user, including\ntheir roles. OpenMRS has no narrower privilege for a user editing their\nown userProperties, which is all the frontend needs here.\n\nVerified by replaying the 68 API endpoints the app calls against four\nrole profiles (registration clerk, clinician, registration supervisor and\nsupervisor+clinical); all pass. OpenMRS caches role privileges in the\nJVM, so this needs a restart to take effect.","tree":{"sha":"0e8d204b3627dba34616375cedd69a50edfba6d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/0e8d204b3627dba34616375cedd69a50edfba6d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e8d204b3627dba34616375cedd69a50edfba6d9\nparent 09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788731352 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788731352 -0700\n\n(fix) Stop the patient chart crashing and restore clinical privileges (#451)\n\n* (fix) Strip disabled frontend modules from the routes registry too\n\nOpening a patient chart crashed the browser tab for non-admin users at\nMatsapha. The renderer died after logging\n\n  Could not find the package @madiro/esm-nutrition-app defined in the\n  current importmap\n\n457,406 times in a single page load.\n\nremove-importmap-entries.groovy deleted the modules named by the\n`modulesToRemove` property from importmap.json but left them declared in\nroutes.registry.json. The deployed build therefore advertised 42 apps\nwhile the importmap could resolve only 39. Matsapha disables three\n(@madiro/esm-mental-health-app, @madiro/esm-nutrition-app and\n@openmrs/esm-ward-app), and the nutrition app registers an extension into\npatient-chart-dashboard-slot - a slot that renders only on the chart,\nwhich is why home and patient search were unaffected and only clicking\nthrough to a patient broke.\n\nThe app-shell retried resolving those packages without bound until the\ntab ran out of memory. Bunia and Mosul use the same script and had the\nsame latent inconsistency.\n\nThe script now strips both files, discards the stale .br/.gz copies\nwritten before the edit (they still held the pre-removal content, so\nnginx could serve an importmap that disagreed with the plain file), and\nfails the build if any app is left declared in routes.registry.json\nwithout an importmap entry.\n\n* (fix) Restore the chart read privileges clinical users need\n\nEvery Matsapha user hit 403s across the patient chart. Fourteen\nprivileges were missing from `General role`:\n\n  Edit Users              recently-viewed patients (regression from #449)\n  Get Allergies           allergies tab\n  Get Conditions          conditions tab\n  Get Diagnoses           visit note diagnoses\n  Get Programs            programs tab\n  Get Patient Programs    programs tab\n  Get Forms               clinical forms list\n  Get Care Settings       orders tab and lab worklists\n  Get Orders              orders tab\n  Get Order Types         ordering\n  Get Order Frequencies   drug ordering\n  Get Encounter Roles     saving a form\n  Get Medication Dispense dispensing\n  Get Notes               visit notes\n\nOnly `Edit Users` was a regression from #449, which moved it to\n`Supervisor`. The other thirteen were never on `General role` - they live\non `General Doctor`, which no Matsapha user holds, because the site''s\nprovisioning script builds flat `Matsapha:` roles instead of using the\ndistro domain roles.\n\n`Patient registration` gains `Add Relationships` so registration clerks\ncan record relationships; the role previously carried no privileges of\nits own.\n\nNote that granting `Edit Users` lets any holder edit any user, including\ntheir roles. OpenMRS has no narrower privilege for a user editing their\nown userProperties, which is all the frontend needs here.\n\nVerified by replaying the 68 API endpoints the app calls against four\nrole profiles (registration clerk, clinician, registration supervisor and\nsupervisor+clinical); all pass. OpenMRS caches role privileges in the\nJVM, so this needs a restart to take effect.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnd/YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHxoQAHU3qWRa+aaMY1eAv1ZNec2t\n45302k9jkR1mnC+BRrbAhwp1/fu8ygsnTp3iFRyCV3P/GBJ3ls/B/UJEhbMXP1bP\nsjL9JG7CXD6ZgWwtMMrHUBfsQDA/mNZzNYmAV9TyORZDFEbGlIgnfkUROCS9CF3f\n1QMp6gNtUtvs8+Ju4gWLLKGPQxyJSBgm6iemyRFQrMeozDMC5nvWiO3PzoSvIzTM\nVkHEulLGH57h+Qmk3PK9LesFJXIr818I2UjEfkjTl4ZhQQzcamGbB/70uqKa1Im2\nGKYVyq6A+hDp221HZBWZxt6xWFxbiXVT4rieSbqEwXyP6BSAVoBr8Af+sIML0nGy\n8hl2Rt1gXq42N74NU+MojWh3R1TfU/I8rptuhvRPERkOJWPokQqy+MKzG3v6Jznm\nIaNKguOGIR2nqqrHHL7B+2DEIjNho2Ngo8uadE9rKmzgdT65G7hkmi4o17qYBirO\n3oeqypelk/K30OPnyws0nWYKDSA49dqHa27V04zw/ANoEYiPF1MaG+rUko3IgsAV\nLrTj9Y+JRbV2loW58tY6nVGjtWKUEuZYl9B6dy7SPKu63qZM5cxGRk4sbFQVQ4BO\nyW+Ny1aVybRreRzIQa4ZfxhCANx6SbGiQh7T93gk73m2C/GFsY4eSw+mUSxMfeTj\nfK7awdiw3QQUNY4Ou0sT\n=w7RA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T21:49:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDE2NjAzYjdmNDIyMDYzMjE4OGI2NzkwMzAzY2UyMWE0MGE2M2U4NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37","sha":"09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37"}],"sha":"16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/16603b7f4220632188b6790303ce21a40a63e85c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:12:32Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:12:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Repair the Playwright workflow and clear the npm advisories (#450)\n\n* (fix) Use Yarn in the Playwright workflow\n\nThe workflow ran `npm ci`, which fails without a package-lock.json - the repo\nhas never had one, only yarn.lock. It is workflow_dispatch only, so the failure\nwould not have shown up unless someone triggered it by hand.\n\nIt matters because run-e2e-tests.yml is workflow_call only and ci.yml''s call to\nit is commented out, leaving this the only way to run the e2e suite today.\n\nSwitches to `yarn install --immutable` with setup-node''s yarn cache, matching\nrun-e2e-tests.yml, and narrows the browser install to chromium, which is all\nplaywright.config.js projects.\n\n* (fix) Bump tar, brace-expansion and ip-address for advisories\n\nClears the 12 open Dependabot alerts on main, which reduce to three transitive\npackages under the Playwright toolchain:\n\n  tar             7.5.13 -> 7.5.22  (6 alerts, incl. critical GHSA-23hp-3jrh-7fpw)\n  brace-expansion 5.0.6  -> 5.0.9   (3 alerts, high)\n  ip-address      10.2.0 -> 10.7.0  (3 alerts, high)\n\nAll three arrive transitively - tar and ip-address under node-gyp via\nsocks-proxy-agent, brace-expansion under minimatch - so `yarn up -R` was used\nand package.json is unchanged. None of them reaches a deployed artifact: the\ndistribution is built from distro/pom.xml and the frontend from\nspa-assemble-config.json, neither of which reads this lockfile. The exposure was\nto developer machines and CI runners installing the e2e dependencies.\n\nVerified with `yarn install --immutable`; Playwright 1.59.1 resolves and all 10\nspecs are still discovered.","tree":{"sha":"791d704c2c3a617defb7c42dfb6d0a9952b3c291","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/791d704c2c3a617defb7c42dfb6d0a9952b3c291"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37","verification":{"payload":"tree 791d704c2c3a617defb7c42dfb6d0a9952b3c291\nparent 55fbc427cffe3acc070e835707b362e7f800af8b\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788531152 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788531152 -0700\n\n(fix) Repair the Playwright workflow and clear the npm advisories (#450)\n\n* (fix) Use Yarn in the Playwright workflow\n\nThe workflow ran `npm ci`, which fails without a package-lock.json - the repo\nhas never had one, only yarn.lock. It is workflow_dispatch only, so the failure\nwould not have shown up unless someone triggered it by hand.\n\nIt matters because run-e2e-tests.yml is workflow_call only and ci.yml''s call to\nit is commented out, leaving this the only way to run the e2e suite today.\n\nSwitches to `yarn install --immutable` with setup-node''s yarn cache, matching\nrun-e2e-tests.yml, and narrows the browser install to chromium, which is all\nplaywright.config.js projects.\n\n* (fix) Bump tar, brace-expansion and ip-address for advisories\n\nClears the 12 open Dependabot alerts on main, which reduce to three transitive\npackages under the Playwright toolchain:\n\n  tar             7.5.13 -> 7.5.22  (6 alerts, incl. critical GHSA-23hp-3jrh-7fpw)\n  brace-expansion 5.0.6  -> 5.0.9   (3 alerts, high)\n  ip-address      10.2.0 -> 10.7.0  (3 alerts, high)\n\nAll three arrive transitively - tar and ip-address under node-gyp via\nsocks-proxy-agent, brace-expansion under minimatch - so `yarn up -R` was used\nand package.json is unchanged. None of them reaches a deployed artifact: the\ndistribution is built from distro/pom.xml and the frontend from\nspa-assemble-config.json, neither of which reads this lockfile. The exposure was\nto developer machines and CI runners installing the e2e dependencies.\n\nVerified with `yarn install --immutable`; Playwright 1.59.1 resolves and all 10\nspecs are still discovered.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmtHQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3qoQAJApr61uFWIFd6+pLldsN247\nS6yWukPIw5ZDYgZy4KZHnLiVrMXcsDoDMfl35TRVBTVu+UA+5kt76I5thkT6d2H9\nUVwSekZaKOiDddUst7VUOvB26450AjBVNBj1Z//56T6SQGSCXcZm/JjtrnrMeLuD\nK4G/99VXSnMzA7jdxCv0xR6heBumoO8mFQcokvydsPHEi2x13W57kxO8ZMb++eKl\nWajL2h+y6HCNxAD5p5ZyZ7on0YPVsAHLF6kQmzOsw68jFI47eiBQLy4cPVqHUv8Z\nnfT1bQyCSy4WGri5iB2VlvWM+TIsmd2rC7Ek+vLidcGLLGLnlGkG167uFGY9GXZ1\nfbLylyOhO4OX1VkSPkd3+0ICsVzC03tYNkPi58jXOO8dOu4VUCwZYfY1EUVA4nZj\n3p9R05KdRP5VEleDPe1lb1UrAEafL3wh+r8ZCKxzTo4XNM+nXZZV+OHIc3uD/MxS\nS0F4jysIZUG8dOVxj3j1eQmhOLYK75CjhZ5xuN7wbEGvBkXHKM7NhM1eMPE0IAfu\nDjMfotIt9zt3ERL+9KuNkS6GL95S8u8ypthBy2xd9dENE4EAVpogoeskhXrj8+UP\n22/T4+aBXSP3HrW3XJqBCAmV+BFn/4EAby6ZPAIRVuSech/QdV+AUNF6t5PMHSkw\nIsbNSKgob9buaKCP9wBo\n=9630\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T14:12:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37","node_id":"C_kwDOLPFUQdoAKDA5YTcyNWZkYzA5ZjNjMzM1YWM0NDM5OWI5ZWFhODI4MWM2NTFlMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commit/55fbc427cffe3acc070e835707b362e7f800af8b","sha":"55fbc427cffe3acc070e835707b362e7f800af8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/55fbc427cffe3acc070e835707b362e7f800af8b"}],"sha":"09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/09a725fdc09f3c335ac44399b9eaa8281c651e37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirupius","id":15266028,"login":"pirupius","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjY2MDI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/55fbc427cffe3acc070e835707b362e7f800af8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:56:33Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:56:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Separate administrative privileges from clinical roles (#449)\n\n`General Doctor` held 77 administrative privileges, and every clinical role in\nthe distro inherits it - Mental Health Counselor/Doctor, Maternity Nurse,\nFamily Planning, Nutrition Clinician, Nutrition Nurse Assistant, Laboratory\nTechnician, Surgery and Anesthesia, Emergency Room, Neonatology, Pediatrics,\nAdult Care, Maternity, Outpatient and Supervisor. Any clinician could therefore\nmanage roles and modules, edit global properties, delete users and reset\npasswords. Filling in a consultation form should not confer that.\n\nThe 77 move to `Supervisor`, in five groups: user and role administration (7),\nsystem administration (8), the HL7 interface (16), metadata management (38) and\ndestructive clinical privileges - Delete Patients/People/Patient Identifiers/\nPatient Programs (4), plus Manage Modules, Manage Global Properties, Delete\nUsers and Edit User Passwords. Get/View Global Properties, View RESTWS and View\nMetadata Via Mapping deliberately stay with `General Doctor`: O3 reads them at\nruntime.\n\n`General role` - which every user holds - granted `Add Users` and `Edit Users`,\nso any receptionist could create accounts. Its own description says it carries\n\"all API privileges except administrative privileges with security\nimplications\". Both removed.\n\nAdds the 22 domain roles the catalogue was missing. 22 of 39 encounter types\nwere gated by View/Edit privileges that no role granted, so those forms were\ninvisible to everyone: HIV, TB, ANC, HBV, HCV, NCD, NTDs, Cervical Cancer,\nGynaecology, Social Work, Referral & Discharge, Palliative care, Travel\nMedicine, Cholera, Snakebite, ICU, POCUS, Blood Transfusion, Pre-Donation,\nRadiology Request, Small Procedure Report and Wound Dressing. Each follows the\nexisting `Family Planning` pattern. Encounter types with no granting role now\nstand at 0, and declared privileges granted by no role at 0 - down from 22 and\n50.\n\n`Supervisor` moves to the end of the file and now inherits all 39 clinical\ndomains rather than 5; it previously could not see Family Planning, Nutrition,\nLaboratory, Surgery, Emergency Room, Neonatology, Pediatrics, Adult Care,\nMaternity or Outpatient forms. The file is dependency-ordered, so it has to sit\nbelow every role it inherits.\n\nNo existing UUID is changed and none is duplicated; the 22 new ones are UUIDv5\nof the role name, so they are reproducible. Only three pre-existing rows change\ncontent - General Doctor, General role and Supervisor - and no role other than\nthose two loses a privilege.","tree":{"sha":"bdb767a42062dfb2f1f3996e413ab752c086fb17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/bdb767a42062dfb2f1f3996e413ab752c086fb17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/55fbc427cffe3acc070e835707b362e7f800af8b","verification":{"payload":"tree bdb767a42062dfb2f1f3996e413ab752c086fb17\nparent c3a7e966e45e76faf692095a9c641c5a7593f5d2\nauthor Pius Rubangakene <piruville@gmail.com> 1788530193 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788530193 -0700\n\n(fix) Separate administrative privileges from clinical roles (#449)\n\n`General Doctor` held 77 administrative privileges, and every clinical role in\nthe distro inherits it - Mental Health Counselor/Doctor, Maternity Nurse,\nFamily Planning, Nutrition Clinician, Nutrition Nurse Assistant, Laboratory\nTechnician, Surgery and Anesthesia, Emergency Room, Neonatology, Pediatrics,\nAdult Care, Maternity, Outpatient and Supervisor. Any clinician could therefore\nmanage roles and modules, edit global properties, delete users and reset\npasswords. Filling in a consultation form should not confer that.\n\nThe 77 move to `Supervisor`, in five groups: user and role administration (7),\nsystem administration (8), the HL7 interface (16), metadata management (38) and\ndestructive clinical privileges - Delete Patients/People/Patient Identifiers/\nPatient Programs (4), plus Manage Modules, Manage Global Properties, Delete\nUsers and Edit User Passwords. Get/View Global Properties, View RESTWS and View\nMetadata Via Mapping deliberately stay with `General Doctor`: O3 reads them at\nruntime.\n\n`General role` - which every user holds - granted `Add Users` and `Edit Users`,\nso any receptionist could create accounts. Its own description says it carries\n\"all API privileges except administrative privileges with security\nimplications\". Both removed.\n\nAdds the 22 domain roles the catalogue was missing. 22 of 39 encounter types\nwere gated by View/Edit privileges that no role granted, so those forms were\ninvisible to everyone: HIV, TB, ANC, HBV, HCV, NCD, NTDs, Cervical Cancer,\nGynaecology, Social Work, Referral & Discharge, Palliative care, Travel\nMedicine, Cholera, Snakebite, ICU, POCUS, Blood Transfusion, Pre-Donation,\nRadiology Request, Small Procedure Report and Wound Dressing. Each follows the\nexisting `Family Planning` pattern. Encounter types with no granting role now\nstand at 0, and declared privileges granted by no role at 0 - down from 22 and\n50.\n\n`Supervisor` moves to the end of the file and now inherits all 39 clinical\ndomains rather than 5; it previously could not see Family Planning, Nutrition,\nLaboratory, Surgery, Emergency Room, Neonatology, Pediatrics, Adult Care,\nMaternity or Outpatient forms. The file is dependency-ordered, so it has to sit\nbelow every role it inherits.\n\nNo existing UUID is changed and none is duplicated; the 22 new ones are UUIDv5\nof the role name, so they are reproducible. Only three pre-existing rows change\ncontent - General Doctor, General role and Supervisor - and no role other than\nthose two loses a privilege.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqms4RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc3AQAA+gJMKLzau+loXZbvKjZNYh\nog1rvdk6L7rvBQJ5VOW1YA22uwIt0GaC+XoxGrvZDsyHlNzoxGjTAwm6C4gMDJtX\nCUh+0s6zN8murZ62znTUHLaiQz1ZCw4IH3W4HOmncyufNIIdWyQWnlCfCGWnSMFe\n6rdnEgwa7MY3RMfpxuGbc2jK4UzI+yS2kuM+zaPM/Ow5/MNSxFAagq7Go4vkIa+g\nT65PimaT4MrhqxPaEZG8s+8F4s5IMc1aubGgsYgMZhNSEPTdIIpPLjCHMquMywAA\nD4Grhu9eVjRiEhyZswPlxgkE+y3tBisFqL+8jkTDW4UiX0y8r/lmFsk2Zypw4XOY\nFRbWjltwk4wRNx