eived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/commits/225eca38cd3d7359bfe2b18b264afdfc79eb47a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T08:14:04Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T08:14:04Z","email":"piruville@gmail.com","name":"Pius Rubangakene"},"message":"(fix) Add graceful shutdown grace periods to openmrs and mysql containers\n\nDocker''s default 10s stop timeout is not enough for Tomcat plus ~40\nmodules and the embedded ActiveMQ broker. A SIGKILL partway through\nshutdown leaves a torn record in the KahaDB journal, and the next boot\nfails in recoverProducerAudit with \"Invalid location ...\nNegativeArraySizeException\".\n\nGive openmrs 120s and mysql 60s. InnoDB recovers from a hard kill on its\nown, but a clean stop avoids a long redo replay on the next start and\nkeeps the binlog tail intact for CDC.","tree":{"sha":"a7f247ba838b4af2fdca8f50979014f777f6f860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/trees/a7f247ba838b4af2fdca8f50979014f777f6f860"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MSF-OCG/LIME-EMR/git/commits/225eca38cd3d7359bfe2b18b264afdfc79eb47a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15266028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirupius/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_