s://api.github.com/users/lkladnit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lkladnit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openshift/networking-console-plugin/commits/123e2fdcb3c5a3cf39be09ccf03546a511cdbce0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:56:47Z","email":"lkladnit@redhat.com","name":"Leon Kladnitsky"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:56:47Z","email":"lkladnit@redhat.com","name":"Leon Kladnitsky"},"message":"OCPNETUI-56: Add ci-test-stack Helm chart for E2E test environments\n\nAdd Helm chart that deploys a networking-console-plugin + OpenShift\nconsole stack for CI E2E testing:\n\nConsole deployment:\n- Off-cluster bridge with bearer-token auth via ServiceAccount\n- SA token Secret for automatic cluster authentication\n- Route for external HTTPS access\n- ClusterRoleBinding for console read access to networking CRDs\n\nPlugin deployment:\n- Nginx-based serving of built plugin assets on port 8080\n- ConfigMap with no-cache headers for plugin-manifest.json/plugin-entry.js\n- Service exposing the plugin to the console\n\nRBAC:\n- Runner RoleBinding for ARC runner namespace-scoped test permissions\n\nConfigurable via values.yaml: plugin image, console image, API server\nURL, i18n namespace, replica count.\n\nUsed by the ci-env-controller (follow-up PR) to provision per-run\ntest environments.\n\nJira: OCPNETUI-56\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd4df1e546b2b0fa188684d19f65b8bc9be155e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openshift/networking-console-plugin/git/trees/cd4df1e546b2b0fa188684d19f65b8bc9be155e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openshift/networking-console-plugin/git/commits/123e2fdcb3c5a3cf39be09ccf03546a511cdbce0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85610882?v=4","events_url":"https://api