":"https://api.github.com/repos/openshift/networking-console-plugin/commits/83b1ba23c23ab2f380e9498bbe236fe03bab9002/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T23:41:28Z","email":"sdickers@redhat.com","name":"Scott J Dickerson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:45:01Z","email":"sdickers@redhat.com","name":"Scott J Dickerson"},"message":"OCPNETUI-58: Add Health and Backend health columns to Services and Routes list pages\n\nSummary of changes:\n\n- Update the `Service` list page to show the health of the service endpoints\n  based on `EndpointSlices` (discovery.k8s.io/v1).\n\n- Update the `Route` list page to show the health of the backend service endpoints\n  based on the `EndpointSlices` (discovery.k8s.io/v1) of the `Service` the `Route`\n  is targeting.\n\n- The `useEndpointHealth` hook watches `EndpointSlices` (discovery.k8s.io/v1)\n  and aggregates endpoint readiness into a `namespace/service` keyed health map.\n\n- Watch hooks that create an aggregated view object to include health status\n  along with the base entity data are used to simplify the component code.\n\n- Specialized row cell components are used to display the health status in the list\n  pages based on the aggregated view object.\n\n- Sorting on the health columns ascending is Healthy -> Degraded -> Down -> Unknown.\n\nSigned-off-by: Scott J Dickerson <sdickers@redhat.com>","tree":{"sha":"afefbad6dcdda72c312fbda51d69b897685ae65d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openshift/networking-console-plugin/git/trees/afefbad6dcdda72c312fbda51d69b897685ae65d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openshift/networking-console-plugin/git/commits/83b1ba23c23ab2f380e9498bbe236fe03bab9002","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3985964?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjd78/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sj